<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="fr">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>{{ "label.maintenance"|trans({}, 'config') }}</title>
    {# Deliberately self-contained page (no external asset: it has to render with the site cut off), hence this local <style>. The nonce is required: as soon as one is present on style-src, 'unsafe-inline' becomes a no-op and a <style> element is authorized by the nonce alone. It is put under a guard because csp_nonce() only exists once a csp: section is configured: without one, the page has to render a bare <style> rather than break at the very moment the site is down #}
    <style {% guard function csp_nonce %}nonce="{{ csp_nonce('style') }}"{% endguard %}>
        body { font-family: sans-serif; display: flex; align-items: center;
               justify-content: center; min-height: 100vh; margin: 0; background: #f5f5f5;
               padding: 1rem; box-sizing: border-box; }
        .box { text-align: center; padding: 2rem; background: white;
               border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.1);
               max-width: 30rem; width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; }
        h1 { color: #333; font-size: 1.5rem; }
        p { color: #666; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="box">
        <h1>🚧 {{ "label.maintenance"|trans({}, 'config') }}</h1>
        <p>{{ "label.maintenance_message"|trans({}, 'config') }}</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>